{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And HaShem said to Moses: this thing too, which you have spoken, I will do.</b> Even though you were nearly despairing of the promise 'I have known you by name,' nevertheless I am turning back from anger and I promise you also this great thing — 'and I will know you by name' — by virtue of finding favor, even though you did not request it from the side of finding favor, for you said only 'make known to me, I pray, Your ways'; nevertheless, since the words 'I have known you by name' issued from your mouth, I will do also this thing for the sake of finding favor, and I will know you by name as at the first."], :book :exodus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:25:07.084064276Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}